      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Carvedilol--a vasodilating beta-blocker has been shown in multicentre trials to be as effective as standard beta-blockers in improving exercise tolerance in patients with angina pectoris and it is more effective than nifedipine. The side effects are less than conventional beta-blockers and nifedipine. Carvedilol is an effective anti-anginal therapy and improves the quality of life."},
